  "architecture_summary": "A screenshot-to-code application using a monorepo structure. The frontend is a React 18 + TypeScript application with Vite for bundling, using Tailwind CSS for styling and Radix UI for accessible components. The backend is a FastAPI Python application that provides REST endpoints and WebSocket support. The core functionality involves uploading screenshots/images or providing text descriptions, which are processed by an AI agent that uses LLM providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini) to generate code. The agent can execute tools to write files, run commands, and modify project structure in real-time, streaming updates back to the frontend via WebSockets. The system also supports image generation via Replicate API and includes an evaluation framework for benchmarking model outputs.",
  "key_patterns": [
    "FastAPI REST API with WebSocket streaming",
    "LLM Provider abstraction with factory pattern",
    "Agent tool-calling execution loop",
    "Prompt pipeline with message builders",
    "SSE (Server-Sent Events) for streaming responses",
    "React Zustand for state management",
    "Radix UI primitive components",
    "Docker containerization for full-stack deployment",
    "Evaluation framework with pairwise comparisons",
    "Image generation via Replicate integration"
  ]
}